---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const path='/intelligence/agent-swarm/';
const description='Six playable worlds exploring how bounded agents coordinate, share uncertain reality, adapt, survive shocks and work without a God’s Eye.';
const content="<div class=\"swarm-lab\"><a class=\"lab-back\" href=\"/intelligence/\">← Intelligence</a><p class=\"lab-kicker\">Agent Swarm Lab / Six worlds · One open question</p><header class=\"lab-hub-hero\"><div><h1>Little minds.<br><em>Large worlds.</em></h1><p>When does intelligence emerge from many bounded, partially informed agents?</p><p class=\"lab-zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">有限的个体，不完整的世界。什么时候，群体真的会更聪明？</p><a class=\"lab-back\" href=\"#six-worlds\">Choose a world ↓</a></div><canvas data-hub-world aria-label=\"An illustrative 3D sketch of the foraging experiment\"></canvas></header><div class=\"lab-manifest\"><div><strong>Enter a small world.</strong><p>Each illustration is driven by an actual simulator. Move through time, inspect a body, and replay the same seed.</p></div><div><strong>Break an assumption.</strong><p>Move the food. Share a false belief. Lose the mother. The interesting result may be the one that refuses your story.</p></div><div><strong>Count what survives.</strong><p>Delivered work, forecast error, memory, energy and messages. A beautiful swarm is a beginning, not an answer.</p></div></div><section id=\"six-worlds\" class=\"lab-tiles\" aria-label=\"Six simulations\"><a class=\"lab-tile\" href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/roach-emergence/\"><span class=\"tiny\"><span>FIELD 01</span><span>land</span></span><canvas data-card-world=\"roach-emergence\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></canvas><h2>Roach Emergence</h2><p>When does local signaling earn its energy cost?</p><span class=\"enter\">Enter the experiment ↗</span></a><a class=\"lab-tile\" href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/shared-reality/\"><span class=\"tiny\"><span>FIELD 02</span><span>beliefs</span></span><canvas data-card-world=\"shared-reality\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></canvas><h2>Shared Reality</h2><p>Can agents agree enough to act without agreeing confidently on a mistake?</p><span class=\"enter\">Enter the experiment ↗</span></a><a class=\"lab-tile\" href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/learn-forget-evolve/\"><span class=\"tiny\"><span>FIELD 03</span><span>evolution</span></span><canvas data-card-world=\"learn-forget-evolve\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></canvas><h2>Learn, Forget, Evolve</h2><p>Can a small policy change adapt to a new world without erasing the old one?</p><span class=\"enter\">Enter the experiment ↗</span></a><a class=\"lab-tile\" href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/asteroid-button/\"><span class=\"tiny\"><span>FIELD 04</span><span>asteroid</span></span><canvas data-card-world=\"asteroid-button\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></canvas><h2>The Asteroid Button</h2><p>Does distributing a fixed budget preserve useful work after correlated damage?</p><span class=\"enter\">Enter the experiment ↗</span></a><a class=\"lab-tile\" href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/ocean-swarm/\"><span class=\"tiny\"><span>FIELD 05</span><span>ocean</span></span><canvas data-card-world=\"ocean-swarm\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></canvas><h2>Ocean Swarm</h2><p>Who repairs the sensing constellation when the sea breaks the plan?</p><span class=\"enter\">Enter the experiment ↗</span></a><a class=\"lab-tile\" href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/minimum-intelligence/\"><span class=\"tiny\"><span>FIELD 06</span><span>frontier</span></span><canvas data-card-world=\"minimum-intelligence\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></canvas><h2>Minimum Intelligence</h2><p>How much model planning earns its place when physical work, information and complexity all count?</p><span class=\"enter\">Enter the experiment ↗</span></a></section><section class=\"lab-section\"><p class=\"tiny\">A laboratory, not a verdict</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>The swarm is allowed to lose.</h2><p>These six experiments follow a single chain: local coordination → shared prediction → bounded adaptation → robustness → physical constraints → the minimum intelligence needed. Controllers and budgets are declared, failures are retained, and the full source and seeded results are inspectable inside each world.</p><p>All environments are synthetic. The three-dimensional sketches illustrate declared models; they do not certify biology, robotics, ocean engineering or general intelligence. Actual model responses, where available, are separated from rule-based simulation.</p><p lang=\"zh-Hans\" class=\"lab-zh\">群体可以输，失败必须留下。六个实验从局部协作、共享预测、有界适应、抗冲击、物理约束，一直追问到最低智能需求。每个世界都有方法、源码与可重播证据。</p><div class=\"lab-links\"><a href=\"/intelligence/swarm-lab/\">The original eight small worlds →</a><a href=\"/intelligence/three-rule-swarm/\">Three Rules, One Lunch →</a><a href=\"/intelligence/one-door/\">One Door, Many Hands →</a></div></div></section></div>";
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'CollectionPage',name:'Agent Swarm Lab',description,url:'https://iamrobin.ai'+path};
---
<BaseLayout title="Agent Swarm Lab — Intelligence — Robin Xie" {path} {description} {schema}>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/agent-swarm/lab.css"/><Fragment set:html={content}/><script is:inline type="module" src="/agent-swarm/hub.mjs"></script>
</BaseLayout>
